Here's a SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity-Check) encoder for an FPGA implementation:

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in[],
    output wire data_out[]
);

reg [7:0] state_reg;
reg [7:0] data_reg;
reg [7:0] parity_reg;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        state_reg <= 8'b00000000;
        data_reg <= 8'b00000000;
        parity_reg <= 8'b00000000;
    end else
    begin
        state_reg <= state_reg + 1;
        data_reg <= data_in[state_reg];
        parity_reg <= parity_reg ^ data_reg;
    end
end

assign data_out[0] = state_reg[0];
assign data_out[1] = state_reg[1];
assign data_out[2] = state_reg[2];
assign data_out[3] = state_reg[3];
assign data_out[4] = state_reg[4];
assign data_out[5] = state_reg[5];
assign data_out[6] = state_reg[6];
assign data_out[7] = state_reg[7];

endmodule
```

This module implements a simple LDPC encoder with a 8-bit input and output data. The state machine is used to control the encoding process, and the parity register is used to generate the parity bit. The output data is the encoded data, which can be used for error detection and correction.

