Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts messages via the Slack API to a specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const url = `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage?token=YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN&channel=${channel}&text=${encodeURIComponent(text)}`;

  fetch(url, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'
    }
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => console.log('Message posted successfully:', data))
    .catch(error => console.error('Error posting message:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Replace `YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN` with your actual Slack API token. You can obtain an API token by following these instructions: https://slack.com/help/articles/1150052681343-Creating-and-using-API-tokens

Also, replace `#general` with the desired channel name or ID. You can find the channel ID by hovering over the channel name in the Slack web interface and looking at the URL in the address bar. The channel ID is the number after `/#`.

This function uses the fetch API to send a POST request to the Slack API with the provided text and channel. It then logs the response data to the console. If there's an error, it logs the error message to the console as well.

Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts a message via the Slack API to the specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = 'https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXXX/XXXXX/XXXXX'; // Replace with your Webhook URL
  const payload = {
    channel,
    text
  };

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => console.log('Message posted to Slack:', data))
    .catch(error => console.error('Error posting to Slack:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Replace `'https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXXX/XXXXX/XXXXX'` with your Webhook URL, which you can find in your Slack app's settings. Also, replace `'#general'` with the channel you want to post the message to.

Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts messages via the Slack API to the specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = `https://hooks.slack.com/services/${process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_ID}/${process.env.SLACK_CHANNEL_ID}`;

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      text,
    }),
  })
    .then((response) => {
      if (response.ok) {
        console.log('Message posted to Slack successfully.');
      } else {
        console.error('Error posting message to Slack:', response.statusText);
      }
    })
    .catch((error) => {
      console.error('Error posting message to Slack:', error);
    });
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Make sure to replace `process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_ID` and `process.env.SLACK_CHANNEL_ID` with your actual Slack webhook ID and channel ID.

