Here's an After Effects script that creates a vertical video by stacking two other videos on top of each other vertically, with the first video on the top. The top half of the video has subtitles placed on the bottom of that video and the text file/script.

```javascript
// Get the project and its assets
var project = app.project;
var assetsFolder = Folder.selectDialog("Select the folder containing your assets:");

// Import the videos and text file
var video1File = assetsFolder.getFile("video1.mp4");
var video2File = assetsFolder.getFile("video2.mp4");
var textFile = assetsFolder.getFile("text.txt");

// Create a new composition
var comp = project.createComposition(640, 1080, 30);

// Import the videos into the composition
comp.importFile(video1File);
comp.importFile(video2File);

// Stack the videos on top of each other vertically
var video1Layer = comp.layers["Video 1"];
var video2Layer = comp.layers["Video 2"];
video1Layer.move(-320, 0); // Move the second video to the left
video2Layer.move(0, 0); // Move the first video to the top

// Add subtitles to the top half of the video
var subtitleText = textFile.read();
var subtitleLayer = comp.layers.addText("Subtitle", "Arial", 24, "#FFFFFF", 1);
subtitleLayer.move(0, -320); // Move the subtitle layer to the bottom
subtitleLayer.selectAllText();
subtitleLayer.setText(subtitleText);

// Export the composition as a video
comp.exportFile("vertical_video.mp4", ExportFormat.MPEG4);
```

