To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. Sign up for an Auth0 account and create a new application.
2. In the Auth0 dashboard, navigate to the "Applications" tab and click on your newly created application.
3. Under the "Settings" tab, click on "SSO" and enable the "SAML" protocol.
4. Download the "SAML metadata" file provided by Auth0.
5. Install the `@auth0/auth0-react` package in each of your React apps using npm or yarn:
```bash
npm install @auth0/auth0-react
```
or
```bash
yarn add @auth0/auth0-react
```
6. In each app, create a new file named `auth0.js` and import the necessary modules:
```javascript
// auth0.js
import { Auth0Provider } from '@auth0/auth0-react';
import auth0Config from './auth0-config.js';

function Auth0Wrapper({ children }) {
  return (
    <Auth0Provider
      domain={auth0Config.domain}
      clientId={auth0Config.clientId}
      redirectUri={auth0Config.redirectUri}
      scope={auth0Config.scope}
    >
      {children}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}

export default Auth0Wrapper;
```
