To help the coffee shop proprietor identify loyal customers based on their purchasing patterns, you can create a PHP program that queries the transaction database using GROUP BY and HAVING clauses to filter and group the data. Here's a sample PHP code:

```php
<?php
// Database connection details
$servername = "localhost";
$username = "username";
$password = "password";
$dbname = "database_name";

// Create connection
$conn = new mysqli($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);

// Check connection
if ($conn->connect_error) {
    die("Connection failed: " . $conn->connect_error);
}

// Query the transaction database for loyal customers
$sql = "SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*) as purchase_count
FROM transactions
WHERE product_id = 'specific_product_id'
GROUP BY customer_id
HAVING purchase_count >= 3";

$result = $conn->query($sql);

// Display the results
if ($result->num_rows > 0) {
    // output data of each row
    while($row = $result->fetch_assoc()) {
        echo "Customer ID: " . $row["customer_id"]. " - Purchase Count: " . $row["purchase_count"]. "<br>";
    }
} else {
    echo "0 results";
}

$conn->close();
?>
```

Replace `'specific_product_id'` with the actual product ID you want to search for. This code will retrieve the customer ID and the number of purchases for each customer who has bought the specified product at least three times within a week. You can then use this information to create a list of loyal customers or take other appropriate actions.

