1. First, make sure you have the JS SDK installed and configured in your project. You can find more information on how to do this in the official documentation: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/javascript-sdk/getting-started

2. Next, create a function that will retrieve the user's session. Here's an example of how you can do this:
```javascript
function getUserSession() {
  // Check if the user is already logged in
  if (FB.getLoginStatus().authResponse) {
    // Get the user's access token
    var accessToken = FB.getLoginStatus().authResponse.accessToken;

    // Create a new request object with the access token
    var request = {
      method: 'GET',
      url: '/me',
      params: {
        access_token: accessToken
      }
    };

    // Make the request to the Graph API
    FB.api(request, function(response) {
      // Handle the response
      console.log('User session:', response);
    });
  } else {
    // The user is not logged in, redirect them to the login page
    FB.login();
  }
}
```
This function first checks if the user is already logged in using the `FB.getLoginStatus()` method. If they are, it retrieves their access token from the `authResponse` object.

Next, it creates a new request object with the access token and makes a GET request to the Graph API using the `FB.api()` method. The request is made to the `/me` endpoint, which returns information about the current user.

Finally, the function handles the response by logging it to the console. If the user is not logged in, the function redirects them to the login page using the `FB.login()` method.

